## 3. Component Architecture & System Modules

### A. Funding Checklist & Category Selector — `FundingChecklist.jsx`, `CategorySelector.jsx`
- Renders 4 tasks with a live progress bar (Framer Motion animated width transition).
- Clicking an incomplete task smoothly scrolls (`scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'})`) to that section — sections are refs, not route changes, to avoid state loss.
- Category pills: D2C, Tech/SaaS, AgTech, MSME/Handicrafts, Healthcare, Services — selected category persists to `businessDetails.category` on save, styled with active/inactive Tailwind variants (not just color swap — include a subtle scale + border transition).

### B. Idea Input & Validation — `IdeaInput.jsx`
- Controlled `<textarea>`, word count computed via a debounced `useMemo` (avoid recalculating on every keystroke render if the idea is long).
- Live badge: `word count / 100 min words`, turns green at 100–300, red outside range.
- Inline warning text exactly as specified, shown only after first blur (don't scold the user before they've typed anything).
- "Scan Schemes 🧭" button disabled + `aria-disabled` until valid range; shows a spinner + "Matching schemes..." while `POST /api/schemes/scan` is in-flight.

### C. Loan Application Generator — `ApplicationModal.jsx`
- Opens from any scheme result card, passing `schemeId` + the saved `businessIdea`.
- Backend drafts a formal application to the Branch Manager, explicitly referencing CGTMSE / Stand-Up India / Mudra guarantees where applicable to that scheme.
- Modal has "Copy Text" (clipboard API, with a toast confirmation) and "Download Application PDF" (generated server-side or via a client PDF lib — pick one, don't duplicate logic in both places).
- Handles the Gemini failure case with a retry button, not a blank modal.

### D. Doc Whisperer PDF Document Scanner — `DocWhisperer.jsx`
- Drag-and-drop zone (react-dropzone or custom) accepting Identity/MSME PDFs only.
- Client-side pre-validation (file type + size) before hitting the network, so bad uploads never reach Multer.
- On upload: Multer stores → `pdf-parse` extracts text → Gemini verifies structure/authenticity → returns structured JSON (`{isValid, docType, extractedFields, flags}`) → auto-ticks `scanIdentityDocs`.
- UI shows the structured verification summary as a readable card, not raw JSON.

### E. BizCalculus P&L Engine — `BizCalculus.jsx`
- Auto-pulls saved `businessIdea` + `category` — user should never have to re-type it.
- Gemini constructs a 1-Year P&L table: Revenue, COGS, Gross Profit, OPEX, Net Profit, Break-even month, and CFO-style advice.
- Rendered as a real table component (sortable/scrollable if long), not a wall of text — plus a small trend chart (Recharts) for Revenue vs Net Profit across the 12 months.
- Auto-ticks `generatePnLPlan` on successful generation; caches the last result in `pnlData` so re-visiting the tab doesn't force a re-generation (add a manual "Regenerate" button instead).

