## 5. Frontend ⇄ Backend Wiring Checklist

- [ ] Central `api/axiosClient.js` with base URL + JWT interceptor — no raw `fetch`/`axios` calls scattered in components.
- [ ] Each module has one hook (`useSchemeScan`, `useDocWhisperer`, `useBizCalculus`) that owns its loading/error/data state — components stay presentational.
- [ ] Checklist progress bar re-fetches (or optimistically updates then reconciles) after every module action completes.
- [ ] No component reads/writes `localStorage` directly for business data — the DB via API is the single source of truth.
- [ ] All Gemini-dependent routes have a visible timeout/fallback UI state (never an infinite spinner).

---

## 6. Definition of Done

A module is "done" only when: the UI state, the API contract, and the Mongoose schema field all agree — and a user can complete that step, refresh the page, and see the checklist item still marked complete.